      "description": "Travel ERP Platform To proceed to the secure customer login page, please click here Critical technical support – 24/7 Phone: +972-3-6076353 For Gilboa service please contact ghelp@galor.com For GILBOA Requirements for Travel Management System click here Website Menu Website Menu Platform ERP Mid-Office Solutions Travel Agents Inbound Tour Operators Outbound Tour Operators Airline Vacation Companies Partners Resources Blog News eBooks Success Stories Company About Us Team Careers Contact EN EN ES עב Get Demo Close Menu Platform ERP Mid-Office Solutions Travel Agents Inbound Tour Operators Outbound Tour Operators Airline Vacation Companies Partners Resources Blog News eBooks Success Stories Company About Us Team Careers Contact Get Demo Travel Booster’s Holistic ERP Technology Revolutionize your business with Travel Booster – the platform built for flexibility and power. Talk to an expert Manage Create Sell Operate & control every aspect of your business. Gain a continuous overview of your profitability and sales. Our automated mid-office tools enable you to manage your day-to-day, analyze your business performance, manage your financial operations, and build your business guidelines. Details of each trip are incorporated into one docket (travel file), including services, suppliers, invoices, travel documents, customer profiles and preferences, and integration with external distribution channels such as GDS. Contact Us Tailored to your unique needs, with limitless possibilities to combine in-house content with externally sourced content. Construct tailor fit products quickly and efficiently with Travel Booster’s industry leading technology which makes it so much easier to create, operate, and customize in-house contracts and allotments for all services, such as flights, hotels, tours, attractions, car rentals, and multiple types of packages – static, dynamic and event-led. Contact Us Leverage and launch online and on-site selling channels, with Travel Booster’s holistic platform. Provide your agents with seamless XML interfaces for searching and booking, all while reaching your customers through desired channels and benefiting from up-selling options, cross-selling options, and a call center. With the ability to build websites for both open and closed user groups, you can manage multiple booking sources from one platform, create proposals, and then sell and distribute with our boosted API. Contact Us TB GI TBGI – Travel Booster Generic Interface In the event that the various integrations available are not sufficient to meet the needs of a Travel Booster user, we have developed a generic interface that enables you to integrate whichever additional content sources you wish into Travel Booster. This interface is called TBGI. All the business rules and capabilities of the system support the unique and private content that is integrated into Travel Booster. TB API Travel Booster’s API In addition to the abundance of UI capabilities that Travel Booster has, each user can also develop their own private UI to suit their needs or integrate with their clients’ systems. This capability is designed to allow Travel Booster to connect to external sales sites and systems of agents or business clients working with the same agency that uses Travel Booster. Our TBAPI also enables synchronization between local distribution systems (LDS) and Travel Booster (Alp and SABRE LDS, for example). B2S - Business to Supplier The B2S configuration is used by travel service providers to upload their products into the Travel Booster system. In addition, the supplier can see all reservations created using their products, and then confirm or reject these reservations. The supplier confirmation or rejection is reflected automatically in the passenger’s travel file (docket). B2E - Business to Employee The B2E configuration is used by company employees to create bookings and manage the customer trip from all aspects. This includes everything having to do with operations, accounting, business rules settings, supplier payments, and more. The B2E user interface is done via web browsers. It is important to note that the entire system is a web-system hosted on the cloud, meaning there is no need for a Legacy system with integration to Web. The entire system is SaaS (Software as a Service) on the Web. B2B - Business to Business The B2B configuration is used by companies that work with travel companies and/or tour operators, including companies who book business travel or travel agents who book tourism and travel services. The B2B configuration also includes B2B4C, which enables you to build “white label” web pages from which you can sell travel products to customers of your clients. B2C - Business to Customer The B2C configuration, used for the sale of all tourism and travel services directly to the passengers themselves, includes upsell capabilities, landing pages, mobile, and more. UI The UI layer is responsible for the inputs and outputs of the system across all channels. The UI is displayed through web browsers, meaning that any device with web browser allows for the use of Travel Booster, including desktop, tablet, and mobile. There are no hardware requirements. Engine The engine layer includes the intelligence of the Travel Booster platform and is responsible for all the calculations and complex operations within the system. It stores all system parameters, flags and constants that define the operation of the system. It is also home to all the business rules that define the relationship between the travel agency and the suppliers, agents, and business customers. Furthermore, the engine layer includes employee incentives, transaction fees, markups, commissions from interface providers, and interfaces. Within the engine layer lay the definitions of internal products including pricing and availability, the ordering mechanism for non-allocated products, and more. The engine is integrated with all GDS’s and external content source",
